### ============================================================================
### Auth.http — Login and authentication diagnostic requests.
###
### Usage:
### 1. Select environment "local" or "azure" (top-right in IDE).
### 2. Run "Login" to get a JWT token.
### 3. Copy the "token" value from the response JSON.
### 4. Paste it into the "token" field in http-client.env.json.
### 5. All subsequent requests use this token for authorization.
### ============================================================================


### ============================================================================
### Login
### POST /api/auth/login — Authenticates user, returns JWT token.
### Copy the "token" field from the response into http-client.env.json.
### ============================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@zcloud.cz",
  "password": "Invoice123"
}

###

### ============================================================================
### Validate Token
### GET /api/auth/validate — Checks if the current token is valid.
### Returns 200 if valid, 401 if expired or invalid.
### ============================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/validate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================================================
### Auth Diagnostic (SysAdmin token required)
### GET /api/diagnostic/auth — Dumps full auth state as seen by the function.
### Shows: Authorization header, User claims, manual JWT validation result.
### Use this to debug role/claim issues on a token that already validates.
### ============================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/diagnostic/auth
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================================================
### Auth Diagnostic (no token) — must be rejected
### Since issue #263 the endpoint is SysAdmin-only, because its payload contains
### the JWT configuration and every claim. Expected: 401, empty body.
### ============================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/diagnostic/auth
